C/ READALL (USA003087 Sec. 22.1) is raw fixed-width card-image input: no
C/ field division, no separators, no conversion. Each CHARACTER item is
C/ filled to its declared maximum length OR to end of line, whichever comes
C/ first; the next item resumes from the next column of the same line. A
C/ second READALL statement advances one line first. Unlike READ (which
C/ splits on whitespace), READALL slices adjacent fixed-width fields that
C/ carry no separator between them. See run_all.sh.
 TRA: PROGRAM;
    DECLARE C1 CHARACTER(3);
    DECLARE C2 CHARACTER(4);
    DECLARE C3 CHARACTER(5);
    READALL(5) C1, C2;
    READALL(5) C3;
    WRITE(6) C1;
    WRITE(6) C2;
    WRITE(6) C3;
 CLOSE TRA;
